Phase 5 Task 5.4 — Preserve Studio provenance and truthful re-synthesis
(bead VieNeuTTSApp-nqx.7.4). Spec AC6: a Studio clip's provenance records the
profile, model revision, language and voice/clone id of the audio it holds, and
a re-synthesis requires the matching active profile — never a silent
substitution by another engine.

Identity:
- `synthesis_context.same_engine(stored, requested)` — the ONE looser rule this
  task adds: same profile wins, and a stored render with no identity is VieNeu
  (the only engine the app had before provenance). Deliberately looser than
  `context_matches` (which still guards caches), because Studio's "Tạo lại"
  intentionally picks a new voice/text/settings: only the ENGINE is fixed.
- `StudioClip.context: SynthesisContext | None = None` (default keeps every old
  construction valid — old projects read as "unknown engine").
- `splice_clip_audio(..., *, context=None)` sets the replaced clip's provenance
  to the engine that produced the new audio; ops are untouched.
- `load_project_from_artifact(path, text, context=None)` stamps every clip with
  the take's identity; `load_project_from_chapters(..., contexts=)` stamps each
  clip from `BookState.contexts` (the audiobook's recorded render provenance),
  so a chapter rendered by Qwen is never read as VieNeu's and vice versa.

Controller:
- `_foreground_context` is set in `_submit_text_job` only after the TTSRequest
  validates, cleared on begin/submit failure, and handed to
  `_complete_foreground_audio(..., context=)` by `_on_terminal`; the committed
  artifact's identity lands in `_current_artifact_context`, which
  `openInStudio` passes to the artifact loader.
- `openChapterInStudio` passes `state.contexts`; both openers call the new
  `_reset_studio_regen()`.
- `studioClips` rows expose `profile` / `profileLabel` / `language` ("" when the
  audio predates provenance) for Phase 6's QML.
- `studioRegenClip` resolves the submission context first, then refuses a
  mismatch with the profile it needs: new string "Đoạn này được tạo bằng
  {profile}. Hãy chuyển sang hồ sơ đó để tạo lại." (translated + asserted in
  test_i18n), plus `studioRegenProfile` / `studioRegenProfileLabel` /
  `studioRegenProfileChanged` and the `studioSwitchToRegenProfile` slot that
  performs the switch the refusal offers.
- Rollback/disarm: a submission that admits no job (closing worker), a
  cancelled job and a failed job all clear the armed splice — including the new
  `_studio_regen_context` — so a later synthesis can never be spliced into a
  clip that did not ask for it.

Tests (+18): test_studio.py TestClipProvenance (unknown default, splice
replaces/clears provenance, artifact + chapter loaders, render ignores
